<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:44:34 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category></category><title>Putin agrees to resume three-way talks with Kyiv and Washington</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/putin-agrees-to-resume-three-way-talks-with-kyiv-and-washington</link><description>
President ⁠Volodymyr Zelenskiy ​said on Wednesday ​that Ukraine supported a US proposal for ​three-way talks ‌with Russia ⁠and the United ‌States at the level ⁠of negotiators to be held as soon ​as possible, preferably ‌no later than early November. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Grégoire Roos, Director of the Europe, Russia and Eurasia Programme at Chatham House, says that "it's not clear whether Putin would meet Trump and Zelensky", adding that "meeting Zelensky is the last thing that Putin would be prepared to do".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a08fd0b8-cd85-11f1-b980-4da0d2c6855d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261021-210107-211150-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a08fd0b8-cd85-11f1-b980-4da0d2c6855d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261021-210107-211150-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a600228c-cd85-11f1-b6ff-d5fb08978532</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:32:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>Trump exploits France riots to push false immigration claims ahead of midterms</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261021-trump-uses-france-riots-to-push-false-immigration-claims-ahead-of-midterms</link><description>
Donald Trump and his inner circle are using unrest in France to push unsubstantiated claims blaming the riots on immigration, even showing French protest footage at midterm rallies. But there is no evidence linking immigration to the unrest, and it's prompted French President Emmanuel Macron to accuse world leaders of making “stupid comments” at France’s expense. Trump’s focus comes as Republicans face mounting pressure ahead of the midterms and his approval rating hits a reported record low.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d5be998-cd83-11f1-80ea-eb48fa034ddc/w:1024/p:16x9/Screenshot-2026-10-21-211315.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d5be998-cd83-11f1-80ea-eb48fa034ddc/w:1024/p:16x9/Screenshot-2026-10-21-211315.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a79e1cd4-cd85-11f1-8f33-95be71b0013f</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:28:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Neither the Sudanese military, nor the RSF take any acknowledgement of human life in this war'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/neither-the-sudanese-military-nor-the-rsf-take-any-acknowledgement-of-human-life-in-this-war</link><description>
The death toll from a drone strike Monday on a market in an area disputed between Sudan and South Sudan has risen to 153 and is likely even higher, a local official told AFP on Wednesday. Authorities in Abyei district said the strike on the Amiet market involved the use of multiple munitions and was carried out by the Sudanese army. FRANCE 24's Mark Owen speaks with Jan Pospisil, Sudan Affairs Analyst at the Peace and Conflict Resolution Evidence Platform. He says that for a long time the Sudanese army has tried "to portray a picture internationally that they are humane, whereas RSF is committing atrocities. Here we see very clearly that there is not much difference between these two".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/303326fa-cd83-11f1-989f-4da0d2c6855d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261021-203844-205016-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/303326fa-cd83-11f1-989f-4da0d2c6855d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261021-203844-205016-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3521d5da-cd83-11f1-ac98-f9a30321d3f0</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:28:21 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Le Pen sees polls boost amid mass protests, riots</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/le-pen-sees-polls-boost-amid-mass-protests-riots</link><description>
Marine Le Pen is set to officially launch her presidential campaign this weekend at the National Rally two-day party congress in Orléans. The latest Ifop poll, carried out in the wake of the mass protests and riots in France, suggests the far right leader would win the first round of the presidential election by a wide margin, and far-left candidate Jean-Luc Melenchon emerged as her most likely opponent in the runoff. FRANCE 24's Emerald Maxwell reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/af09a82a-79ee-11f1-a43e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-04T210557Z-856145428-RC267MACOHTM-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-POLITICS-FARRIGHT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/af09a82a-79ee-11f1-a43e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-04T210557Z-856145428-RC267MACOHTM-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-POLITICS-FARRIGHT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">86bc9326-cd7e-11f1-b79c-f9a4acde9b65</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:56:02 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Trump faces fresh questions over ties to 'humanitarian' Putin</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/trump-faces-fresh-questions-over-ties-to-humanitarian-putin</link><description>
US President Donald Trump's pivot away from Ukraine has triggered fresh questions about his attachment to Russian leader Vladimir Putin, the man a top American envoy flattered on Wednesday as a "humanitarian. Trump has cast his dealings with Putin as part of a mega-deal that has secured the release of American detainee Stephen Hubbard -- and which Trump says will end Russia's war on Ukraine. FRANCE 24's Gulliver Cragg reports from Kharkiv.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6eda9058-cd3f-11f1-84de-8bea73bbe173/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-21T102625Z-722811654-RC2M7OATXY8O-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-PUTIN-WITKOFF.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6eda9058-cd3f-11f1-84de-8bea73bbe173/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-21T102625Z-722811654-RC2M7OATXY8O-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-PUTIN-WITKOFF.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9bd68316-cd7e-11f1-8b2e-9de24ce4507a</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:53:28 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Culture</category><title>Canadian publisher drops author Orelien after confirming he used AI in debut novel</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/culture/20261021-canadian-publisher-drops-author-orelien-after-confirming-he-used-ai-in-debut-novel</link><description>
The Canadian publisher representing Thélyson Orélien on Wednesday said it had dropped the prize-nominated writer over new information indicating that he did use artificial intelligence to write his acclaimed debut.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cffc09d6-b744-11f1-8522-4d7b41827f6c/w:1024/p:16x9/Mod%C3%A8le-1920-x-1080-14-2.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cffc09d6-b744-11f1-8522-4d7b41827f6c/w:1024/p:16x9/Mod%C3%A8le-1920-x-1080-14-2.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">698e1f92-cd72-11f1-974b-2b96b0d62b41</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 17:32:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cffc09d6-b744-11f1-8522-4d7b41827f6c/w:1024/p:16x9/Mod%C3%A8le-1920-x-1080-14-2.png">© Joel Saget, AFP/ File picture</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Macron visits Riyadh to show solidarity amid Houthi attacks, ease tensions at home via fuel deal</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/macron-visits-riyadh-show-solidarity-amid-houthi-attacks-ease-tensions-home-via-fuel-deal</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron on Wednesday paid an unannounced visit to Riyadh in a bid to underscore French support for the kingdom amid intensified attacks by Houthi rebels and an attempt to ease tensions at home by securing oil and diesel imports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/aa979f94-cd6e-11f1-b444-4da0d2c6855d/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-21T151836Z-1599925537-RC2O7OAFE3Q9-RTRMADP-3-GULF-FRANCE-SAUDI-ARABIA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/aa979f94-cd6e-11f1-b444-4da0d2c6855d/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-21T151836Z-1599925537-RC2O7OAFE3Q9-RTRMADP-3-GULF-FRANCE-SAUDI-ARABIA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">437b552a-cd6f-11f1-b38d-a5ce92c5d5e6</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 17:09:37 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/aa979f94-cd6e-11f1-b444-4da0d2c6855d/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-21T151836Z-1599925537-RC2O7OAFE3Q9-RTRMADP-3-GULF-FRANCE-SAUDI-ARABIA.jpg">© Benoit Tessier, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Greece: Protesters draw inspiration from demonstrations in France</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-greece-protesters-draw-inspiration-from-demonstrations-in-france</link><description>
 Inspired by protests in France and other parts of Europe, thousands of Greek students on Wednesday demonstrated around the country.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/be60282c-cd6c-11f1-bbb1-4da0d2c6855d/w:1024/p:16x9/Greece-protests-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/be60282c-cd6c-11f1-bbb1-4da0d2c6855d/w:1024/p:16x9/Greece-protests-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f94cfa70-cd6a-11f1-8aee-f524bda5d4ee</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:31:49 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>World set to breach 1.5°C warming limit set by Paris Climate Agreement</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-world-set-to-breach-1-5%C2%B0c-warming-limit-set-by-paris-climate-agreement</link><description>
The UN is warning that global commitments to cut planet-heating emissions are falling far short of the Paris climate goals of 1.5 degrees Celsius warming – and put the world on course for 2.6C warming this century. The report by the United Nations Environment Programme lays bare the chasm between rhetoric and action when it comes to tackling global warming, and the challenge before political leaders at November's COP31 climate summit - set to take place next month in Turkey. Story by Emerald Maxwell.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d071a7de-cd67-11f1-9ca4-eb48fa034ddc/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26233615918833.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d071a7de-cd67-11f1-9ca4-eb48fa034ddc/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26233615918833.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">291bbd04-cd66-11f1-a014-4b1424b6eb3e</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:56:42 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>French President Macron lands in Saudi Arabia on surprise 'solidarity' visit</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/french-president-macron-lands-in-saudi-arabia-on-surprise-solidarity-visit</link><description>
⁠French President Emmanuel ​Macron landed in Riyadh on Wednseday, ‌adding an ⁠unscheduled stop to his ‌ongoing tour of the Gulf ⁠region. The president's office said the visit aimed to demonstrate “France's solidarity” ​with Saudi Arabia in ‌the face of attacks launched by the ‌Houthis against its territory. Details by FRANCE 24 international affairs editor Douglas Herbert.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7a3707c4-cd67-11f1-aaa1-19980254bb31/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-21T142140Z-1388011539-RC2P7OA2A64V-RTRMADP-3-GULF-FRANCE-SAUDI-ARABIA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7a3707c4-cd67-11f1-aaa1-19980254bb31/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-21T142140Z-1388011539-RC2P7OA2A64V-RTRMADP-3-GULF-FRANCE-SAUDI-ARABIA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a12ac1b0-cd65-11f1-b94f-15fe03609a5d</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:54:08 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Kremlin says 'ready' to resume 3-way talks with US and Ukraine mid-November</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/kremlin-says-ready-to-resume-3-way-talks-with-us-and-ukraine-mid-november</link><description>
Moscow is ready to resume trilateral US-Ukraine-Russia talks next month, the Kremlin said Wednesday after President Vladimir Putin met with US envoy Steve Witkoff in Russia. FRANCE 24's correspondent Gulliver Cragg has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0898c536-cd66-11f1-87a1-4da0d2c6855d/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-404e6bea.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0898c536-cd66-11f1-87a1-4da0d2c6855d/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-404e6bea.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a66a2d8c-cd65-11f1-b496-070ec108d2c5</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:51:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Macron rejects Trump’s claims blaming migrants for French riots</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-macron-rejects-trump-s-claims-blaming-migrants-for-french-riots</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron condemned comments by "foreign leaders" on the violent protests in France on October 17. He has now arrived in Saudi Arabia as part of his Gulf tour.
 

</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0fd76160-cd64-11f1-a6ff-19980254bb31/w:1024/p:16x9/Macron-Trump-EN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0fd76160-cd64-11f1-a6ff-19980254bb31/w:1024/p:16x9/Macron-Trump-EN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ee45c502-cd61-11f1-a123-8b211923ec3e</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:29:48 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France: Far right leader Marine Le Pen gains popularity amid nationwide riots</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france-far-right-leader-marine-le-pen-gains-popularity-amid-nationwide-riots</link><description>
Prime Minister Sebastien Lecornu met with union leaders today in France. His government admitted law enforcement officers had lost control this past weekend during protests which resulted in scenes of violence and looting. The country is bracing for more protests – the Yellow Vest movement called on demonstrators to take to the street on Saturday. As the events unfold, far-right leader Marine Le Pen is gaining popularity. Details and analysis by FRANCE 24 international affairs editor Rochelle Ferguson Bouyahi.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2977666a-cd64-11f1-88a0-8bea73bbe173/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-20T134734Z-875218610-RC217OA8MNVB-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-POLITICS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2977666a-cd64-11f1-88a0-8bea73bbe173/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-20T134734Z-875218610-RC217OA8MNVB-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-POLITICS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f19b84b8-cd51-11f1-a5c9-71e16327f734</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:29:42 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Some Brazilians long associated with the left now shift towards Flavio Bolsonaro</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-some-brazilians-long-associated-with-the-left-now-shift-towards-flavio-bolsonaro</link><description>
In the first round of Brazil’s presidential elections, Flavio Bolsonaro got the most votes in 15 electoral districts in the North Zone of Rio de Janeiro, compared with 9 for Lula. This part of the city, long associated with the left and the social policies of Lula’s Workers’ Party, is now shifting towards former president Jair Bolsonaro’s son.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/449179c4-c088-11f1-8ee6-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26277433106719.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/449179c4-c088-11f1-8ee6-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26277433106719.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">64824c74-cd5b-11f1-a1e4-a34bccdf8451</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:28:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Down to Earth</category><title>70% of water produced in Guadeloupe never reaches homes</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/down-to-earth/20261021-70-of-water-produced-in-guadeloupe-never-reaches-homes</link><description>
In the French overseas territory of Guadeloupe, a water crisis is a daily reality, with some residents going without water for weeks. The network is being repaired, but at the current pace, France's Court of Auditors says replacing all of it would take 208 years. Now, a judicial investigation has been opened in Paris into the crisis, following a citizen-led legal action. Our France 2 colleagues report.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/73bb1904-c965-11f1-baa6-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/Capture-d-e%CC%81cran-2026-10-16-a%CC%80-13-04-30.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/73bb1904-c965-11f1-baa6-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/Capture-d-e%CC%81cran-2026-10-16-a%CC%80-13-04-30.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b2ced36e-cd2b-11f1-a18e-39ac91462dff</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:26:19 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE 2</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Italy: Giorgia Meloni approves tougher anti-riot laws after Milan violence 🇮🇹</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-italy-giorgia-meloni-approves-tougher-anti-riot-laws-after-milan-violence-%F0%9F%87%AE%F0%9F%87%B9</link><description>
Italy approved a raft of security measures on Tuesday including a new offence of violent participation in a demonstration, tougher penalties for rioters, and financial liability for parents whose children take part in vandalism and looting.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7740755a-cd62-11f1-be77-eb48fa034ddc/w:1024/p:16x9/Italy-2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7740755a-cd62-11f1-be77-eb48fa034ddc/w:1024/p:16x9/Italy-2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ea733afc-cd4a-11f1-924d-11a0658004fb</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:18:08 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Prosecutors search European Parliament offices of far-right Patriots bloc in graft probe</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261021-prosecutors-search-european-parliament-offices-of-far-right-patriots-bloc-in-graft-probe</link><description>
