</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d6a56ec-cd5e-11f1-9158-4da0d2c6855d/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3VA8TC.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d6a56ec-cd5e-11f1-9158-4da0d2c6855d/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3VA8TC.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">848639a2-cd5d-11f1-9ff0-2763b7931541</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:07:45 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d6a56ec-cd5e-11f1-9158-4da0d2c6855d/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3VA8TC.jpg">© Romeo Boetzle, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>arts24</category><title>Film show: Olivia Colman, Alexander Skarsgård star in horny feminist fantasy 'Wicker'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261021-film-show-olivia-colman-alexander-skarsg%C3%A5rd-star-in-horny-feminist-fantasy-wicker</link><description>
Film critic Emma Jones and Dheepthika Laurent discuss the week's film releases. Olivia Colman and Alexander Skarsgård play an odd couple in the fantasy romance "Wicker" about love, society and the patriarchy. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a478d868-cd59-11f1-90bf-ab78a7fed2ce/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-b22372b6.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a478d868-cd59-11f1-90bf-ab78a7fed2ce/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-b22372b6.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">66678122-cd5a-11f1-88b9-6373f5f897f1</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:54:58 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Dheepthika LAURENT</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Ukraine and Russia both ready to resume trilateral talks with US</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261021-zelensky-proposes-freezing-front-with-russia-first-step-peace-talks</link><description>
Ukraine and Russia on Wednesday said they are both ready to resume trilateral talks with the United States. The news comes after US envoy Steve Witkoff separately met with Volodymyr Zelensky and Vladimir Putin on two consecutive days.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/db40dab2-cd86-11f1-9894-eb48fa034ddc/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26294433555896.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/db40dab2-cd86-11f1-9894-eb48fa034ddc/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26294433555896.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">77ea6e36-cd56-11f1-b1e5-3b7fd4ebe015</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:46:44 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/db40dab2-cd86-11f1-9894-eb48fa034ddc/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26294433555896.jpg">© Kristina Solovyova, Sputnik, Kremlin Pool Photo via AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Peter Zalmayev: 'Ukraine was showing all sorts of cards that Trump took away and gave to Putin'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-ukraine-was-showing-all-sorts-of-cards-that-trump-took-away-from-ukraine-and-gave-to-putin-1</link><description>
Angela Diffley is pleased to welcome Peter Zalmayev, Founder and Director of the Eurasia Democracy Initiative, LIVE from Kyiv. And he warns, "I'm seeing, I'm smelling a Yalta II. I'm smelling another Munich (1938), where we're seeing appeasement of the aggressor." Ukraine faces the possibility that its sovereignty and security could become mere bargaining chips in an era Zalmayev describes as great-power "collusion". He delivers a forceful critique of the Trump administration's approach to Russia, arguing that Washington is weakening Ukraine's negotiating position while offering Vladimir Putin little incentive to abandon his maximalist demands. At stake, he suggests, are the cohesion of the transatlantic alliance, and the credibility of Western security commitments.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dd778d3c-cd5c-11f1-83c4-8bea73bbe173/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261021-152316-153456-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dd778d3c-cd5c-11f1-83c4-8bea73bbe173/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261021-152316-153456-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e355ddbc-cd5c-11f1-83fb-51ed59c64853</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:44:11 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Pain au Chocolat: The sweet story behind a French breakfast icon</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/pain-au-chocolat-the-sweet-story-behind-a-french-breakfast-icon</link><description>
