France is bracing for yet another weekend of protests by high school students and the "Yellow Vest" movement. The government says they're increasing security and personnel to trying to mitigate any violence or chaos. Story by Ophelie Jacobson and France 2.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e10d4d08-cd5a-11f1-a8ab-19980254bb31/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261021-151201-151338-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e10d4d08-cd5a-11f1-a8ab-19980254bb31/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261021-151201-151338-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e6da3854-cd5a-11f1-a291-5f1ed545633a</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:27:21 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Greece: Protesters demand increased funding for public education</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/greece-protesters-demand-increased-funding-for-public-education</link><description>
Students, teachers and civil servants are demonstrating in Greece today, protesting over staff shortages, poor infrastructure and the cost of living. Dozens of students have set up tents in the Square facing Parliament, in Athens, and on a pedestrian street in Thessaloniki on Tuesday. Details by FRANCE 24 correspondent in Athens, Nathalie Savaricas.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d9bcbde0-cd5a-11f1-89c8-ab78a7fed2ce/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-21T123954Z-770228045-RC2K7OA8CUCO-RTRMADP-3-GREECE-PROTEST-STUDENTS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d9bcbde0-cd5a-11f1-89c8-ab78a7fed2ce/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-21T123954Z-770228045-RC2K7OA8CUCO-RTRMADP-3-GREECE-PROTEST-STUDENTS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c9d5e304-cd58-11f1-b3c8-1d1fb528eca6</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:25:12 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>'I didn’t know it was theft': Trials begin in Paris following October 17 violence</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261021-i-didn-t-know-it-was-theft-trials-begin-paris-following-october-17-violence</link><description>
Those arrested during the October 17 rallies filed into the dock at Paris’s Judicial Court on Tuesday, accused of a broad range of offences – from assault against police officers to resisting arrest and handling stolen goods. The courtroom’s charged atmosphere was palpable amid the justice minister’s call for the law to respond with “utmost firmness”.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d3ccd6d4-ccdf-11f1-9378-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3L26JY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d3ccd6d4-ccdf-11f1-9378-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3L26JY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1aff982e-cd4f-11f1-b610-51658bb72136</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:15:24 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d3ccd6d4-ccdf-11f1-9378-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3L26JY.jpg">© Kiran Ridley, AFP</source><dc:creator>David RICH</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
